************************* Capacity Estimation ************************



Just like before throwing a house part, we estimate 
how many guestes
how much food
time management
how manu house help req, 

so we do all these estimations before organizing a party to reduce last minute chaos.

so similarly , in system design also we do capacity estimation
where we predict or determine the max load or demand that a system can handle with its operations parameters.


Factors :
-Hardware resources
processors , memory , storage 
and these are limited
-Software efficiency
-Workload (variation in workload like its will be normal on normal days but workload can spike on a sale day )
-User Behaviour (eg users use insta more at the night time) so we have to measure user behaviour and based on that we do the system capacity
-Performance Matrix 
-Failure Scenarios (eg we have one very heavy AOI and during sale it can fail or db went down etc)




Certain Mterics which we consider for the capacity estimation :

1.Daily Active Users
2.Queries Per Second
3.Storage Requirements
4.Error Rates
5.Response Time
6.Peak Load Handling



Methods & Techniques used for capacity estimation :

1.Traffic : key metrics -> DAU and QPS from above
2.Forecasting : using past traffic data to predict future trends
3.Stress Testing : We intentionally give fake req and overload the system to see how it reacts.
4.Load Testing : we gradually increase the number of rq or load to test and monitor to check how system is performing
5.Capacity planning tools : 


Components of Capacity :
1.CPU : 
processing power, clock speed, number of cores it has
our cpu capacity can be estimated
2.Memory 
3.Storage/DB
4.Network Bandwidth



